- action(n1, "start"): Fails to reflect the documented initial behavior "please register your participation for the event."
- action(n3, "Register post-seminar request"): Missing an outgoing precedence edge to an end node, violating the source requirement "Once you have registered a post-seminar request, the process will come to an end."
- precedence(e1, n8): Places an end node before action(n8, "Register post-seminar request"), contradicting source chronology which states registration occurs after the approved notification and then terminates the process.
- defines(v1, "Is there a fee?", {}) and defines(v2, "Check purchase request approval status", {}): Ranges are empty {}, failing to capture the explicit decision values required by the source ("no fee"/"there is a fee"; "approved"/"rejected").
- branch(b1, XOR) and branch(b2, XOR): Lack guard statements linking the branches to variables v1 and v2, leaving the control-flow choices undefined against the source conditions ("If there is no fee...", "If it is approved...").

